<title>UK: Inchcape H1 profit flat, payout cut to 4.2p.</title>
<headline>Inchcape H1 profit flat, payout cut to 4.2p.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.0		    vs 0.2 loss</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 4.2		    vs 6.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     82.8		   vs 83.3</p>
<p> Turnover		   3,161.8		vs 3,129.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts were for pre-tax profits in a range between 73 and 88 million stg, with the payout seen at between 4.0 and 4.3 pence per share.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 101.8		  vs 48.9</p>
<p> Net exceptional charge 7.5		    vs 9.2 charge</p>
<p> Interest paid	    19.0		   vs 21.1</p>
<p> Tax			  29.1		   vs 27.2</p>
<p> Net taxed	 profit 46.2		   vs 8.6 loss</p>
<p> Retained	  profit 10.8		   vs 52.3 loss</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 12</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 8</p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 30</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the interim dividend of 4.2 pence per share will be paid as a foreign income dividend of 5.25 pence.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
